// The other direction. `e` followed by U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT is two
// code points and one cell, so a caret padded per code point lands too far
// RIGHT -- one column per accent on the line. The three accents below are
// spelled DECOMPOSED in the source on purpose: the precomposed `é` is one
// code point and would not show the bug.
print("résuméé" + nope);
